## 4. Operational Challenges & Mitigations

| Common Challenge | Real-World Impact | Defensive Solution |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **System Downtime Concerns** | Critical business applications cannot be restarted during work hours. | Schedule predictable maintenance windows during off-peak hours with HA failover. |
| **Legacy / End-of-Life Software** | Vendors no longer issue patches for legacy OS environments. | Isolate legacy machines into restricted network VLANs; apply virtual patching via IPS. |
| **Patch Conflict / System Instability** | Updates cause software incompatibility crashes. | Maintain strict pre-deployment staging tests and enforce snapshot rollback points. |

---

## 5. 7-Step Enterprise Implementation Checklist
1. Maintain an automated software asset discovery inventory.
2. Establish strict Patch SLAs (e.g., Critical CVSS 9.0+ patched within 14 days).
3. Automate Windows OS updates via WSUS / Microsoft Intune and Linux via Ansible/yum-cron.
4. Disable legacy protocols (like SMBv1) across the network domain.
5. Create automated system snapshots or backups prior to patching sessions.
6. Conduct monthly vulnerability scans to identify missing third-party patches.
7. Perform an annual review of the organization's patch management policy.

